nk: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\n2: 2, A: 2, J: 2, 9: 2, 8: 1, 7: 1, 6: 1, 4: 3, 3: 1\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♥Q\nsingle: ♣K\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation: I have two single cards available: ♥Q and ♣K, which are valid to play. The previous play was ♣J, so I need to beat that. I should consider which single card is stronger or can set up a better strategy for the game.\n\nReason: The ranking of single cards is from 3 up to red joker. So, in terms of value, ♣K is higher than ♥Q. Playing ♣K would be more advantageous as it\'s a stronger single card and could give me more leverage in future plays. Additionally, I should aim to support my teammate\'s strategy if needed, but since my teammate has only 3 cards, I can focus on my own play to contribute to the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣K"]}'}
